    <string name="header_report">Report a problem</string>
    <string name="header_deck_left">%1$d cards left in the deck</string>
    <!--
      The header badge is a *button*, and its name says so. The felt's draw pile already
      says "N cards left in the deck"; when the badge said it too, a screen reader met the
      same sentence twice on one screen and neither instance said that one of them opens an
      explanation. The pile is the thing being counted, so it keeps the count; the badge is
      the thing that answers "what does that number mean", so it says that instead — while
      still carrying the number it visibly shows, which is what a spoken name must do.
    -->
    <string name="header_deck_badge">%1$d in the deck — what that means</string>

    <!-- What the deck count means, when it is asked. -->
