    <string name="signal_turn">A green ring on a seat</string>
    <string name="signal_turn_meaning">Whose turn it is. It flashes as the turn arrives, because three bots can take theirs between one tap and the next.</string>
    <string name="signal_vinto">A gold ring</string>
    <string name="signal_vinto_meaning">That player has called Vinto. Nobody may touch their cards for the rest of the round.</string>
    <string name="signal_penalty">A red ring, and a hand that flinches</string>
    <string name="signal_penalty_meaning">A penalty card just landed there — a wrong guess, or a wrong toss-in.</string>
    <string name="signal_coalition">A blue ring</string>
    <string name="signal_coalition_meaning">The coalition: everybody except the Vinto caller, playing their last turn together against that one hand.</string>
    <string name="signal_live">A gold ring on the discard</string>
    <string name="signal_live_meaning">That card was put down without its action being used, so the next player may take it and play it instead of drawing. A card whose action *was* played has no ring.</string>
    <string name="signal_tappable">A card that breathes</string>
    <string name="signal_tappable_meaning">It can be touched right now. If nothing breathes, the table is waiting on somebody else.</string>
    <string name="signal_reshuffle">Cards sweeping back into the deck</string>
    <string name="signal_reshuffle_meaning">The deck ran out, so the pile was shuffled back into it. Everything anybody had learned from watching that pile is now out of date.</string>
    <string name="signal_peek">A card that lifts towards the middle</string>
    <string name="signal_peek_meaning">Somebody is looking at it. Everyone sees *which* card was looked at — only the player entitled to it sees the face.</string>

